# elo.env.example — every figure the reserve's own launch needs, in one place.
#
#   cp elo.env.example elo.env        # elo.env IS gitignored (`*.env`).
#                                     # Put the key in the environment, never here.
#   ./launch_elo.sh check             # tooling, chain, and WHICH FACTORY
#   ./launch_elo.sh preflight         # every pons gate, on the wallet that signs
#   ./launch_elo.sh size              # what the opening buy does to the price
#   ./launch_elo.sh plan              # the pinned, unsigned transaction
#   ./launch_elo.sh launch --arm      # THE ONE TRANSACTION
#
# The order these are used in is docs/launch/ONE-SHOT.md §7 and
# docs/launch/ELO-LAUNCH.md §5. This file is the figures; those are the
# ceremony, and they say which steps cannot be undone.
#
# ⚠ PRIVATE_KEY IS NOT IN THIS FILE AND MUST NOT BE ADDED TO IT. `launch_elo.sh`
#   reads it from the environment and never echoes it. A key in a file next to a
#   template named .example is exactly the habit .gitignore's secret block exists
#   to catch, and the catch is second-line — it is not a plan.
#
# LEGEND, and it is the only thing here that really matters:
#
#   [WELDED]  fixed by the launch transaction. No setter exists, at any price.
#   [TIMELOCK] changeable later, behind CREATOR_FEE_RECIPIENT_TIMELOCK.
#   [LOCAL]   read by this script only; changes nothing on chain.
#
# Anything still marked <UNSPOKEN> has no operator sentence in docs/SENTENCES.md
# and is left BLANK on purpose. `launch_elo.sh knobs` REFUSES on a blank welded
# field rather than defaulting it — because a welded figure that lands on its
# recommendation by accident is indistinguishable, afterwards, from one somebody
# chose. That is not a hypothetical here: `hive.env.example` staged SEAT_SCRY as
# the coin being retired, nothing would have failed, and the seat's whole
# economic engine would have welded to a dead token (ONE-SHOT.md §1).

# ── the chain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `cast chain-id --rpc-url $RPC` answers 4663 on this endpoint.
RPC=https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com
# ⚠ FOR THE BROADCAST, PREFER A KEYED PROVIDER. The public endpoint 403s from the
#   box for some methods and is rate-limited for everyone. RUNBOOK.md §209:
#     RPC="$(printf '%s' "$SCRY_RH_RPC_POOL" | cut -d, -f1)"   # from keys.env
# PRIVATE_KEY — export it in your shell. Not here. See above.

# ── who signs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [LOCAL, but it decides a WELDED value] The wallet that broadcasts. It is
# checked against `canLaunch(deployer)` in preflight, it is the CREATE2
# namespace for the salt, and it is the default creator fee recipient. It must
# be the address PRIVATE_KEY controls — `launch_elo.sh` derives the key's own
# address and refuses if they disagree, because a preflight run against one
# wallet and a broadcast from another checks nothing.
# ⭐ SPOKEN 2026-08-21 — the operator's launch wallet, key held on the VM
#   (HELD-KEYS.md row 3j; it supersedes row 3i's never-funded 0xB1ab…B0A7).
#   Same wallet does the opening buy atomically and collects the fees.
ELO_DEPLOYER=0x969D646804D7B911971414C19023a11656Efaee6

# ── the token ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠ [WELDED] EVERY CHARACTER BELOW IS PART OF THE CREATE2 PREIMAGE. The token's
#   creation code carries name, symbol, logo, description, socials, deployer,
#   curve, factory and supply — so one character of the description changes the
#   token's address. Freeze this whole block before mining any vanity salt, or
#   throw the mining away (meter/launch.py `_default_salt`).
ELO_NAME="Elo Pros"
ELO_SYMBOL=ELO
# [WELDED] Metadata the factory records at launch, read back by getTokenInfo().
#
# ⚠ THE LOGO IS ANSWERED — the URL below, and it is the only field in this block
#   that is. The mark is the Nu: the seat the Elo Pros collection uses as its own
#   face, the same picture `EloSeatArt.emblemSvg()` draws on chain and the same
#   one the site, the tab icon and the share card now carry (operator, 2026-08-20:
#   *"make a new ELO logo and use an ELO PRO nft image for our logo"*).
#   `watchtower/art/make_logo.py` renders it; `--check` fails if it drifts.
#
# ⚠ THE STRING IS WELDED AND THE PIXELS ARE NOT, and the two get confused in the
#   expensive direction. This URL is in the CREATE2 preimage, so one character of
#   it changes ELO's address and it can never be edited after the broadcast —
#   every aggregator card reads it forever. The FILE it points at is ordinary
#   static content: re-render it whenever. So the rule is `never move or rename
#   elo-mark-512.png`, not `never touch the art`.
#
# ⚠ 512x512 AND OPAQUE ON PURPOSE. A transparent token logo gets drawn against a
#   background we do not pick, and the Nu's outer contour is bone — on a white
#   card it thins to a pale blob. This one carries the store's own ground so it
#   looks the same on every aggregator. `elo-mark-256.png` is the same picture
#   for anything that wants a lighter asset; it is NOT what goes here.
ELO_LOGO=https://elopros.com/art/elo-mark-512.png
# ⚠ [WELDED] THE EVERGREEN RULE: this string outlives every launch phase — it
#   is on the aggregator card in year three, so it may not mention graduation,
#   the mint, a price, a date, or anything else that is true for a season. The
#   platform's structure is the only thing safe to weld: one reserve, many game
#   coins, a store. Staged 2026-08-21 (operator: *"work on a description to
#   really cook"*); rewrite freely until the broadcast — after it, never.
ELO_DESCRIPTION="One coin, every game. ELO is the reserve of Elo Pros — the game store with a market under it. Every title on the shelf brings its own coin, and every one of them trades against ELO: the road into every game's economy, and the road out."
ELO_WEBSITE=https://elopros.com
# ⭐ SPOKEN 2026-08-21. Welded like the description; blank stays legal for the
#   two that have no handle — a welded empty beats a welded wrong.
ELO_TWITTER=https://x.com/ELOPROS1337
ELO_TELEGRAM=https://t.me/elopros4life
ELO_DISCORD=
ELO_FARCASTER=

# ── the quote asset ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [WELDED] Blank = native ETH, which is the common case and what ELO-LAUNCH.md
# §5 step 2 says to take unless there is a reason. An ERC-20 here must be on
# pons' `approvedPairTokens` list AND changes the shape of the transaction: the
# launch fee travels as value and the opening buy is PULLED, so the asset must
# be approved to the router first. `launch_elo.sh` prints that approve command
# rather than assuming it was run.
#
# ⚠ `approvedPairTokens(0x0)` reads FALSE for native and that is NOT a refusal —
#   a native launch takes its phantom reserve and threshold from the launch
#   config instead. The preflight checks the approval list only for an ERC-20.
ELO_PAIR_TOKEN=

# ── the launch config ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [WELDED] Which of the factory's configs fixes supply, curve fee, phantom
# reserve, graduation threshold, pool fee tier and tick spacing. Configs are
# append-only so an id is stable forever, but an existing one can be EDITED or
# DISABLED by pons' owner — which is what the economics pin is for. At last read
# `launchConfigCount()` was 1, so 0 was the only one. Re-read it; do not quote
# that. `./launch_elo.sh preflight` prints the live config in full.
ELO_LAUNCH_CONFIG_ID=0

# ── the four welded knobs, and none of them has a default ────────────────────

# ⚠ [WELDED? — DISPUTED, 2026-08-17] <UNSPOKEN — ONE-SHOT.md §8 item 2>
#   WHO OWNS OUR FEE TIMING. `sweepFees` refuses a CREATOR's call with
#   `InternalSwapRequiresOperator` whenever the sweep needs an internal swap,
#   which is any time a buyback must execute. `true` hands sweep timing to pons'
#   operator; `false` keeps it ours. ONE-SHOT.md §3b recommends **false**: the
#   whole downstream fee economy — splitter → bank → cistern — assumes we sweep
#   on our own clock. Write `true` or `false`. Blank is refused, NOT read as false.
#
#   ⚠ THE REPO AND PONS' OWN OVERVIEW DISAGREE ABOUT WHETHER THIS IS WELDED.
#   This repo calls it immutable in four places (ELO-LAUNCH.md §1 and §5 step 2,
#   ONE-SHOT.md §6f and §8, and `fees.py`'s header: "set at launch and
#   immutable"). pons' v2 overview lists it as one of exactly TWO things a
#   creator can still change: *"The creator can turn buybacks on or off… pons
#   can turn it off but never on."* Nothing in this tree carries a setter
#   selector to check that against.
#
#   ⭐ RESOLVED 2026-08-21, BY THE READ THIS NOTE ASKED FOR:
#   `setBuybackEnabled(address,bool)` is on the VERIFIED factory ABI, so it is
#   a SETTER, not a weld — pons' docs were right and ELO-LAUNCH.md §1's
#   "no setter" row was wrong (corrected same day). What it is: pons spending a
#   slice of the CREATOR'S OWN fee share buying ELO back into a 5-year vest.
#   `false` because our fee stream already has a posted job — the 1/14 daily
#   buyback through our own splitter (meter/buyback.py) — and because with
#   buybacks on, every sweep that must execute one needs pons' operator
#   (InternalSwapRequiresOperator), handing them our sweep timing. Per pons'
#   docs only the creator can ever turn it ON, so false today forecloses
#   nothing.
ELO_BUYBACK_ENABLED=false

# ⚠ [WELDED] **SPOKEN — 100 bps** (SENTENCES.md 2026-08-17). Tagged <UNSPOKEN> until
#   2026-08-18, which broke this file's own legend two lines from the answer.
#   It is still left BLANK on purpose — see the note further down: a welded figure
#   gets typed by the person signing. Blank-and-refuse, not unspoken.
#   THE ONE KNOB THAT CAN CHARGE
#   ABOVE 1% ANYWHERE, because it is not bounded by Uniswap's tier list the way
#   a pool is. Capped by `maxCreatorTaxBps()` — preflight reads the ceiling and
#   refuses locally rather than letting the launch revert `CreatorTaxTooHigh`.
#
#   ⛔ ONE-SHOT.md §3b-b's 125 recommendation is SUPERSEDED and struck there. It is
#   quoted here only so a reader who greps 125 finds the strike. DO NOT WRITE 125.
#
#   ⚠ THE ANSWER IS 100, AND IT IS SPOKEN (SENTENCES.md 2026-08-17):
#   **2% total, which makes the creator tax 100 bps.** The 100 bps curve fee is
#   pons' launch config and not ours, so 100 here is what makes the total 2%.
#   Reaffirmed against Steam's 30% and ordinary 5%+ sales tax — operator: *"id
#   do less but seemed kinda moot in the end of the day."*
#
#   ⚠ IT IS STILL LEFT BLANK ON PURPOSE, and that is not an oversight. A welded
#   figure gets typed by the person signing, every time. `knobs` refuses a blank
#   rather than defaulting it, which is the whole guard — see the legend above.
#
#   ⚠ THE RATE DOES NOT CHANGE AT GRADUATION. The pool is created with its own
#   fee at zero and the hook charges `hookFeeBps` instead, which pons documents
#   as netting out the same: *"you pay the same rate whether the token is on its
#   curve or in its Uniswap pool."* `./launch_elo.sh fees <ref>` confirms it on
#   chain in one call — a check, not an open question.
#
#   ⚠ AND IT CAN NEVER BE CHANGED. There is no setter, at any price. The
#   operator asked for no locked-in taxes (2026-08-17) and this is the one
#   field that cannot give it. What stays adjustable is everything DOWNSTREAM —
#   `setSplit` with no timelock, the cistern's three knobs, the gacha toll, and
#   all four copy-sale prices.
#
#   ⚠ And note what it does NOT buy: the redistribution pipe does not exist. The
#   creator leg pays ETH; the splitter, bank and cistern are all reserve-
#   denominated. Until that loop runs under a posted rule, no surface may
#   advertise fee-sharing (CLAUDE.md: a card advertising a reward the rule
#   cannot pay is a bug).
ELO_CREATOR_TAX_BPS=

# ⚠ [WELDED, and it is the only reserve the treasury ever gets for free]
#   **SPOKEN IN SCOPE — ~$500** (SENTENCES.md 2026-08-17); the exact wei is what is
#   open, and `size` computes it. Tagged <UNSPOKEN> until 2026-08-18.
#   THE OPENING BUY, IN ETH.
#   pons launches a fixed supply into a curve: there is no creator allocation
#   and no minter, so every unit of the reserve the treasury will ever spend —
#   on a pool seed, on an orchard pot, on anything — is bought on our own curve
#   at market. Anything downstream that assumes a treasury balance has to name
#   where it came from, and the answer is always "we bought it."
#
#   **A zero opening buy is a choice, not a default** (ELO-LAUNCH.md §4). Write
#   `0` deliberately if that is the call. Blank is refused.
#
#   Size it with `./launch_elo.sh size`, against the graduation threshold rather
#   than a dollar figure. Two facts that plan gets wrong in opposite directions:
#   a buy multiplies the marginal price by ((Q + net) / Q)², so the move is the
#   SQUARE of the reserve's growth; and graduating costs
#   threshold / (1 − fee − tax) GROSS, not the threshold.
ELO_OPENING_BUY_ETH=

# ⚠ [TIMELOCK] Who earns the launch's fees, in ETH. This is the one field that is
#   NOT welded — it transfers behind CREATOR_FEE_RECIPIENT_TIMELOCK — but its
#   FIRST value is set by this transaction. Blank defaults to the deployer.
#
#   ⚠ ONE-SHOT.md §6g: the dev wallet and the house wallet are the same address
#   and nothing separates them. Splitting them costs one address, and it is far
#   cheaper before a third-party listing exists than after.
# ⭐ SPOKEN 2026-08-21 — the launch wallet itself. [TIMELOCK] so this is the
#   one address here that can move later: `transferCreatorFeeRecipient` can
#   repoint fee accrual at a cold wallet once revenue is real, and doing that
#   moves the buyback-vest beneficiary with it.
ELO_CREATOR_FEE_RECIPIENT=0x969D646804D7B911971414C19023a11656Efaee6

# ── the opening buy's shape ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [LOCAL] Slippage bound on the opening buy, in whole tokens. `size` prints the
# quoted fill; take a few percent under it. Zero accepts any fill, which on the
# atomic path is defensible (nothing can trade before us in the same
# transaction) and on the non-atomic path is not.
ELO_MIN_TOKENS_OUT=0

# [WELDED] Who receives the opening buy's tokens. Blank = the deployer. The
# recipient is auto-exempted from the opening snipe tax.
ELO_BUY_RECIPIENT=

# ⚠ [WELDED] EXEMPTIONS ARE FIXED AT CREATION AND THERE IS NO ADDING ONE LATER.
#   Comma-separated addresses exempt from the opening snipe tax, for a team
#   bundling opening buys across several wallets. At most 32 on a direct launch,
#   31 through the atomic router (it appends the buy's recipient itself), past
#   which the factory reverts `ExemptionListTooLong`. The launching address and
#   the creator fee recipient are exempted for you, so a solo creator needs
#   nothing here.
#
#   ⚠ Any wallet that will buy inside the snipe window must be on this list. The
#   tax opens near 99% and decays to zero across a few seconds — and at 101ms
#   blocks that window is TENS OF BLOCKS wide, not one or two.
ELO_SNIPE_EXEMPTIONS=

# [LOCAL] Take the atomic launch-and-buy router (default) or launch directly.
# `launchAndBuy` closes the gap where anyone may buy in front of the creator at
# the opening price. It gates its own callers with `onlyPermittedLauncher`,
# which is a DIFFERENT permission from the factory's — being allowed to launch
# does not mean being allowed to launch atomically.
#
# Non-atomic is a priced inconvenience, not a hole (ONE-SHOT.md §3c): a
# front-runner in the gap pays the 90%+ snipe tax for the privilege. If the
# router refuses this wallet, set this to `false` and send the buy immediately
# after. Ignored when the opening buy is 0.
ELO_ATOMIC=true

# [WELDED] The salt that picks the token's CREATE2 address. Blank = a fresh
# random one, domain-separated per deployer, which is right for an ordinary
# launch. A mined vanity salt goes here — and is mined LAST, after every knob
# and every character above is frozen (see the token block).
ELO_SALT=

# ── sizing and rate helpers (LOCAL — none of these reaches the chain) ────────

# [LOCAL] The total a trader pays, in bps, that `./launch_elo.sh fees` sizes the
# creator tax against. 200 = 2% (SENTENCES.md 2026-08-17).
#
# A trader pays `feeBps + creatorTaxBps`, and feeBps comes from PONS' launch
# config (100 bps at last read) — it is not ours to set. So 2% total is a
# creator tax of 100.
#
# The rate does not change at graduation. The pool is created with its own fee
# set to zero and the HOOK charges `hookFeeBps` instead, which is why two
# separate fields exist; pons documents them as netting out the same:
# *"you pay the same rate whether the token is on its curve or in its Uniswap
# pool."* `fees` reads both off a live launch to confirm that on chain rather
# than from their prose — a one-line check, not an open question.
ELO_TOTAL_TRADE_BPS=200

# [LOCAL] A reference launch for `./launch_elo.sh fees`. ELO has no fee policy
# until it exists, so the rates it would inherit are read off any live pons v2
# token. Prefer one that is GRADUATED (phase 2) and charges a nonzero creator
# tax — that combination is also the on-chain confirmation that a creator tax
# rides the hook rather than dying with the curve.
ELO_FEE_REF=

# [LOCAL] Your ETH/USD rate, for `./launch_elo.sh size --usd`. **Nothing in this
# repo fetches a price** and that is deliberate: a rate a script guessed, folded
# into a welded value field, is the failure TICKET.md §8d exists for. Read it
# wherever you normally would, pass it, and read the ETH figure back digit by
# digit before it goes in ELO_OPENING_BUY_ETH above.
ELO_ETH_USD=

# ── the guard ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [LOCAL] `launch --arm` refuses to broadcast until this reads exactly the
# symbol above. It is the typed confirmation against the failure TICKET.md §8d
# exists for: a miscounted zero in a value field, against a tape, that nothing
# on chain objects to. Leave it blank between runs.
ELO_CONFIRM=
